{"name":"Caramel Ice","hex":"#eec9aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"caramel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smooth, chewy, sticky confection made by heating sugar and other ingredients until the sugars polymerize and become sticky.","A (sometimes hardened) piece of this confection."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow-brown color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caramel"},{"term":"ice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Icelandic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water in frozen (solid) form.","Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caramel","blocks":[{"text":"Caramel is a range of food ingredients made by heating sugars to high temperatures. It is used as a flavoring in puddings and desserts, as a filling in bonbons or candy bars, as a topping for ice cream and custard, and as a colorant commonly used in drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Caramel-2.jpg/330px-Caramel-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caramel","wikidata":"Q183440"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?u